WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:06.940
Hey youtuber’s it’s charlie Happy Thanksgiving.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.510
I hope you’ve all had a chance to see the
Doctor Who 50th Anniversary episode.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:13.629
Because so much of the show’s history was
incorporated into it I thought it would be

00:00:13.629 --> 00:00:14.820
fun to go on an easter egg hunt.

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:17.120
Since there are so many I broke this video
into two parts.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.800
Be sure to subscribe to get part 2 I’ll
be posting it on Saturday.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.002
I’ll also be doing a video next week analyzing
some of the bigger theories about who exactly

00:00:22.002 --> 00:00:23.250
the Peter Capaldi Doctor will be.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:25.730
Now these easter eggs are in chronological
order of appearance.

00:00:25.730 --> 00:00:29.440
Since they span the television series, audio
adventures and comic books I’ll include

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.720
a reference for where things can be found.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:32.720
Here we go.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:33.720
1.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:35.370
The Title sequence from the first season of
Doctor who in 1963.

00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:36.550
(TV Show, Season 1 1963)

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:37.550
2.

00:00:37.550 --> 00:00:39.990
The sign Totter’s Lane was where the William
Hartnell Doctor hid his tardis after fleeing

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:41.980
gallifrey with his granddaughter susan foreman.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:42.980
(TV Show, same)

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:43.980
3.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:45.130
I.M Foreman was a gallifreyan monk living
on earth after being driven out by Rassilon’s

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:46.130
Intuitive Revolution.

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:49.460
He formed a traveling show using 13 different
aspects from all of his regenerations and

00:00:49.460 --> 00:00:51.510
crossed paths with Sarah Jane Smith and the
third doctor.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:52.600
( Interference Book 1 &amp; 2 1999)

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:53.600
4.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:54.600
Ian Chesterton.

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.300
One of the Doctor’s earliest companions
from the very first episode.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.219
He later became a science teacher at Coal
Hill in the 1960s.

00:00:59.219 --> 00:01:01.329
He went on to have future adventures with
the fifth and eleventh doctors.

00:01:01.329 --> 00:01:02.329
5.

00:01:02.329 --> 00:01:03.329
W Coburn.

00:01:03.329 --> 00:01:05.000
Anthony Coburn was the writer of the very
first Doctor Who episode.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.000
An Unearthly child.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.000
6.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:08.189
No More is written on Clara’s blackboard.

00:01:08.189 --> 00:01:09.189
7.

00:01:09.189 --> 00:01:13.689
The Clock reads 5:15PM That was the time the
first episode of doctor who aired.

00:01:13.689 --> 00:01:14.689
8.

00:01:14.689 --> 00:01:15.689
The motorbike.

00:01:15.689 --> 00:01:18.749
Clara riding it into the tardis is something
the doctor did during the tv movie.

00:01:18.749 --> 00:01:19.749
9.

00:01:19.749 --> 00:01:21.700
Clara closes the doors to the tardis by snapping
her fingers.

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:23.819
Something only river song used to be able
to do.

00:01:23.819 --> 00:01:24.819
10.

00:01:24.819 --> 00:01:25.819
Cocktails on the Moon.

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:28.619
There is a UNIT Base on the moon manned by
Elizabeth Shaw (sarah jane adventures, the

00:01:28.619 --> 00:01:29.619
death of the doctor).

00:01:29.619 --> 00:01:30.619
11.

00:01:30.619 --> 00:01:31.619
Osgood’s scarf.

00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:32.619
This is the fourth doctor’s scarf.

00:01:32.619 --> 00:01:36.170
Osgood is Kate Stewart’s daughter, who in
turn got the scarf from her father who got

00:01:36.170 --> 00:01:37.799
it from the fourth doctor.

00:01:37.799 --> 00:01:40.490
Who looks mysteriously like the museum curator.

00:01:40.490 --> 00:01:41.490
12.

00:01:41.490 --> 00:01:43.729
The doctor hangs outside of the tardis while
it flies over london monuments.

00:01:43.729 --> 00:01:45.119
Just like in matt smith’s first full episode
the eleventh hour.

00:01:45.119 --> 00:01:46.119
13.

00:01:46.119 --> 00:01:47.119
The 3D Painting.

00:01:47.119 --> 00:01:48.119
No More, Gallifrey Falls.

00:01:48.119 --> 00:01:51.209
The 3D aspect and the plot device, saving
bits of things frozen in spacetime is from

00:01:51.209 --> 00:01:53.360
the episode Nightmare of eden from the fourth
doctor’s run.

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:54.969
Who looks mysteriously like the museum curator.

00:01:54.969 --> 00:01:55.969
Yet again…

00:01:55.969 --> 00:01:56.969
14.

00:01:56.969 --> 00:01:57.969
A Weapon with a conscience.

00:01:57.969 --> 00:02:01.009
This is a reference to a douglas adams story
Life The Universe and Everything.

00:02:01.009 --> 00:02:05.270
It was also an idea they were going to use
for a Tom Baker doctor who movie during the

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:09.590
4th doctor’s run.

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:11.030
15.

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:12.030
Bad Wolf.

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:15.480
Billie Piper is actually playing Bad Wolf,
she’s playing the living conscience of The

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:16.500
Moment device.

00:02:16.500 --> 00:02:19.560
But her appearance is a nod to super goddess
Rose Tyler from series 1.

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:20.560
Sentient Time Lord Technology is also a reference
to Idris.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:21.560
16.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:22.560
The Clockwork of the Moment.

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:24.450
Is a nice reference to the repair bots from
Girl in the Fireplace.

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:25.450
17.

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:26.450
The horse.

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:29.060
Is a nod to Arthur, Tennant’s horse from
Girl in the Fireplace.

00:02:29.060 --> 00:02:32.180
Allons-y is tennant’s famous doctor’s
call to action.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:35.140
But he has said it means two different things.

00:02:35.140 --> 00:02:39.441
One it’s french for “let’s go” and
two he said during the end of time that it

00:02:39.441 --> 00:02:41.900
was a world of consolation to the soul in
times of need.

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:44.660
So it’s kind of like 10s spiritual chicken
soup.

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:45.660
18.

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:46.660
I’m not english.

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:48.390
David tennant is one of the scottish doctors.

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:49.710
So is peter capaldi.

00:02:49.710 --> 00:02:50.710
19.

00:02:50.710 --> 00:02:51.710
Tennant’s costume.

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:56.540
The outfit he’s wearing is from Series 2,
but the physical costume is one he also took

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:58.550
home after his run on doctor who ended.

00:02:58.550 --> 00:03:01.130
Because they didn’t have that many replicas
when it came time to film.

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:04.710
They had to use the one he had kept from way
way back.

00:03:04.710 --> 00:03:07.070
He kept one copy of each piece of clothing
10 ever wore.

00:03:07.070 --> 00:03:08.070
20.

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:09.070
The Timey Wimey Detector.

00:03:09.070 --> 00:03:11.610
It was first used by David Tennant in the
episode Blink.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:16.200
Later tennant makes a joke at Matt Smith’s
doctor using the term Timey Wimey and says

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:18.460
he has no idea where he gets it from.

00:03:18.460 --> 00:03:19.460
21.

00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:20.460
Zygons.

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:22.730
They first appeared in the original UNIT story
from Tom Baker’s run Terror of the Zygons.

00:03:22.730 --> 00:03:26.570
I think they decided to use UNIT and Kate
Stewart in the episode first and as a result

00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:31.720
found it appropriate to use the Zygons as
a nice callback to classic who and Tom Baker.

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:32.720
22.

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:35.310
I’m going to be King.

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:39.740
They did get married and the doctor never
did die technically.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:43.069
So in reality Matt Smith’s doctor has a
legitimate claim to the throne.

00:03:43.069 --> 00:03:44.069
23.

00:03:44.069 --> 00:03:45.600
The 5ish doctors stone statues.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:49.000
In Peter Davison’s parody documentary the
5ish doctors.

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:54.930
the surviving classic doctors try to get into
the 50th anniversary episode and end up becoming

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:57.730
the figures underneath the white cloths pretending
to be statues.

00:03:57.730 --> 00:03:58.730
24.

00:03:58.730 --> 00:03:59.730
The Blowfish.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:03.540
They were creatures from the episode Kiss
Kiss Bang Bang on torchwood.

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:04.610
25.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:05.610
The Fez.

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:10.050
It shows up many times in the episode, but
originally came from the second doctor in

00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:14.730
the episode Evil of the Daleks which is one
of the infamous lost episodes.

00:04:14.730 --> 00:04:15.730
26.

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:21.080
The cybermen painting is a callback to the
original mondas cybermen design from classic

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:22.080
who.

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:23.080
27.

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:24.080
Overcompensating?

00:04:24.080 --> 00:04:27.210
The joke tennant makes is that Matt Smith’s
doctor is “overcompensating” with a flashier

00:04:27.210 --> 00:04:29.490
sonic because regeneration is a lottery.

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:32.099
Implying 12 didn’t get the luck of the draw.

00:04:32.099 --> 00:04:35.800
But after watching the prequel Night of The
Doctor we know that regeneration doesn’t

00:04:35.800 --> 00:04:36.800
have to be random.

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:37.800
28.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:38.800
Codename Chroma 70s or 80s.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:46.229
This is a reference to one the chroma restoration
of a lot of black and white doctor who episodes.

00:04:46.229 --> 00:04:50.969
The 70s or 80s is a reference to the Third
Doctor’s years which were supposed to be

00:04:50.969 --> 00:04:55.740
set in the 80s, but because they were filming
in the 1970s, a lot of 70s references always

00:04:55.740 --> 00:04:56.740
made it into those episodes incorrectly.

00:04:56.740 --> 00:04:57.740
29.

00:04:57.740 --> 00:04:58.740
Reverse the polarity.

00:04:58.740 --> 00:04:59.740
Is another phrase coined by the third doctor.

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:00.740
30.

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:01.740
I think there’s three of them now.

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:02.740
Kate stewart answers “there’s a precedent
for that.

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:03.740
She’s talking about the first anniversary
special.

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:04.740
The three doctors.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:06.780
It was done on the 10th anniversary.

00:05:06.780 --> 00:05:07.780
31.

00:05:07.780 --> 00:05:08.780
The Black Archive.

00:05:08.780 --> 00:05:11.960
The archive was created with the help of the
second or third doctor and has been visited

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:14.680
by Sarah Jane Smith and Martha Jones before
the events of this special.

00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:17.499
It’s like UNITs version of the time vaults
on gallifrey.

00:05:17.499 --> 00:05:18.499
32.

00:05:18.499 --> 00:05:19.499
The wall of fame.

00:05:19.499 --> 00:05:24.880
UNIT keeps tabs on the doctor and all his
companions, so everybody from the doctor’s

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:29.319
past is somewhere on the wall here.

00:05:29.319 --> 00:05:30.319
33.

00:05:30.319 --> 00:05:31.680
Captain Jack’s vortex manipulator.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:34.130
UNIT took it off him after one of his more
recent deaths.

00:05:34.130 --> 00:05:37.979
It’s hard to guess which, because after
his most recent death in Miracle Day he used

00:05:37.979 --> 00:05:40.479
a vortex manipulator to travel off world.

00:05:40.479 --> 00:05:45.099
So that’s it for the first half of the special.

00:05:45.099 --> 00:05:48.039
Be sure to write any extras in the comments
below or if you know any more cool facts about

00:05:48.039 --> 00:05:49.039
one in particular.

00:05:49.039 --> 00:05:50.919
Like I said, part two will post on saturday.

00:05:50.919 --> 00:05:52.599
Be sure to subscribe to get it.

00:05:52.599 --> 00:05:57.590
I’ve also got a game of thrones and legend
of korra book 3 video coming Friday so you

00:05:57.590 --> 00:06:00.110
can watch those on your phones while you’re
out buying stuff.

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:04.370
Right now click here for my review of the
50th and click here for that part 2 video.

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:06.879
I’ll add the annotation after the video
posts on saturday.

00:06:06.879 --> 00:06:10.199
Thanks for watching, happy thanksgiving high
fives!

